- captaind supports a single CLN node
  Nobody runs captaind with more than one CLN node, so `[[cln_array]]` has
  one entry everywhere. captaind refuses to start with the old
  `[[cln_array]]` config. Update the captaind config before you upgrade:
  - Rename `[[cln_array]]` to `[cln]`.
  - Remove the `priority` field.
  - Replace the JSON env var `BARK_SERVER__CLN_ARRAY` with one env var per
    field, for example `BARK_SERVER__CLN__URI` and
    `BARK_SERVER__CLN__HOLD_INVOICE__URI`.

  ```toml
  [cln]
  uri = "https://cln:9736"
  server_cert_path = "/data/cln/regtest/ca.pem"
  client_cert_path = "/data/cln/regtest/client.pem"
  client_key_path = "/data/cln/regtest/client-key.pem"
  hold_invoice.uri = "https://cln:9988"
  hold_invoice.server_cert_path = "/data/cln/regtest/hold/ca.pem"
  hold_invoice.client_cert_path = "/data/cln/regtest/hold/client.pem"
  hold_invoice.client_key_path = "/data/cln/regtest/hold/client-key.pem"
  ```
  [#2857](https://gitlab.com/ark-bitcoin/bark/-/merge_requests/2857)
  - **BREAKING:** The `[[cln_array]]` config section is replaced by `[cln]`.
  - **BREAKING:** The admin RPCs `StartLightningNode` and
    `StopLightningNode` are removed.
